sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant API as eval-hub API Server<br/>:8080 HTTP/HTTPS<br/>TLS 1.2-1.3
    participant Middleware as Identity Middleware<br/>X-User / X-Tenant
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / SQLite<br/>SQL Storage
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>:6443 HTTPS
    participant Init as eval-runtime-init<br/>Init Container
    participant S3 as S3-compatible Storage<br/>HTTPS
    participant Sidecar as eval-runtime-sidecar<br/>Sidecar Proxy
    participant MLflow as MLflow Tracking Server<br/>HTTP/HTTPS
    participant OTel as OpenTelemetry Collector<br/>OTLP/gRPC

    Note over Client, API: Evaluation Job Submission Flow

    Client->>API: POST /api/v1/evaluations/jobs<br/>Headers: X-User, X-Tenant
    API->>Middleware: Validate identity headers
    Middleware-->>API: Identity confirmed

    API->>DB: Store evaluation job record
    DB-->>API: Job ID

    API->>K8s: GET HardwareProfile CR<br/>infrastructure.opendatahub.io/v1
    K8s-->>API: Resource requirements

    API->>K8s: CREATE ConfigMap<br/>Job configuration
    K8s-->>API: ConfigMap created

    API->>K8s: CREATE Job (batch/v1)<br/>init: eval-runtime-init<br/>sidecar: eval-runtime-sidecar
    K8s-->>API: Job created

    API-->>Client: 201 Created (Job ID)

    Note over Init, S3: Evaluation Pod Startup

    Init->>S3: Download test data artifacts<br/>AWS SDK v2
    S3-->>Init: Test data files
    Init-->>K8s: Init container complete

    Note over Sidecar: Evaluation Execution

    Sidecar->>Sidecar: Manage evaluation lifecycle
    Sidecar->>MLflow: Report experiment results<br/>Optional TLS + token auth
    MLflow-->>Sidecar: Tracking acknowledgment

    Note over API, OTel: Observability

    API->>OTel: Export traces, metrics, logs<br/>OTLP/gRPC
    API->>API: Expose /metrics<br/>Prometheus scrape

    Note over Client, API: Collection & Provider Management

    Client->>API: GET /api/v1/evaluations/collections
    API->>Middleware: Validate identity headers
    API->>DB: Query collections
    DB-->>API: Collection data
    API-->>Client: 200 OK (collections)

    Client->>API: GET /api/v1/health
    Note right of API: No identity check required
    API-->>Client: 200 OK (health status)
